From c524aba53f822f9f84be65d4ee031d05dad56be3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felicitas Pojtinger <felicitas@pojtinger.com>
Date: Wed, 05 Aug 2026 23:54:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Add custom SELinux rules to allow Caddy to listen on TCP and UDP listeners via socket activation

Signed-off-by: Felicitas Pojtinger <felicitas@pojtinger.com>
---
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 0f06b2b3ad5b979c58b16459e9540b13212ff04f..7afa6f97bd80456226e007222d0cc739d300a007 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -31,6 +31,22 @@ $ ssh setup@2a01:4f8:c015:706c::1
 [setup@vanlug-forgejo-runner ~]$ sudo journalctl _SYSTEMD_USER_UNIT=forgejo-runner.service -f
 ```
 
+To update the SELinux policies for the containers (`.cil` files), run:
+
+```shell
+$ ssh setup@vanlug.p8.lu
+[setup@vanlug-main ~]$ sudo -iu caddy podman inspect caddy | sudo udica caddy
+$ scp setup@vanlug.p8.lu:/home/setup/caddy.cil caddy.cil
+```
+
+You'll then need to manually edit the CIL file (see https://github.com/SELinuxProject/selinux-notebook/blob/main/src/cil_overview.md for a guide) for any additional capabilities the container might need. You can see the denials by running the following:
+
+```shell
+[setup@vanlug-main ~]$ sudo ausearch -m avc -ts recent --input-logs
+[setup@vanlug-main ~]$ sudo semodule -DB # To show any denials hidden by `dontaudit` rules
+[setup@vanlug-main ~]$ sudo semodule -B # To re-enable the `dontaudit` rules
+```
+
